Package: secondbrain
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: bouliehaan <debus.jacob@gmail.com>
Depends: nodejs (>= 22.21.1), lightdm, openbox, chrony, curl, picom, unclutter,
 x11-xserver-utils, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Recommends: chromium
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/bouliehaan/secondbrain
Description: wall-mounted dashboard for a headless kiosk display
 Drives a wall-mounted display through LightDM, Openbox and Chromium in kiosk
 mode: calendar, weather, Google Voice messages, important mail, package
 shipments, Transmission downloads, what samo-radio is playing, and a
 drip-the-faucets freeze alert.
 .
 The package owns the display side -- the service user, the systemd unit, the
 LightDM autologin drop-in, the kiosk supervisor and the clock. Credentials are
 never shipped; they go in /etc/magicmirror-secondbrain/ and the package
 creates that directory but never writes into it.
 .
 It is not a container, because it drives a real display through a real X
 session.
